# Build context for this Dockerfile is apps/api, so every pattern below is
# relative to apps/api.
#
# Nothing listed here is needed by `nest build` (which compiles src/ via
# tsconfig.build.json) or by `node dist/main` at runtime. Excluding these keeps
# build context small and, more importantly, stops a developer's local
# node_modules or a stale local dist/ from being copied into the image, where it
# could shadow the correct platform-specific install.

# --- dependencies and build output -----------------------------------------
# A host node_modules may contain Windows/macOS binaries and would be wrong on
# Linux. The image installs its own inside the build.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- test and coverage ------------------------------------------------------
# tsconfig.build.json already excludes test/ and **/*spec.ts from compilation.
test/
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# --- secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Never bake credentials into an image layer. Unlike .gitignore, this excludes
# .env.example too: a template has no business in a build context, and keeping
# the rule unconditional removes any chance of a negation line re-admitting one.
.env
.env.*

# --- VCS and CI -------------------------------------------------------------
# Present at the repository root rather than in apps/api, listed defensively so
# this file stays correct if the context is ever widened.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# --- tests, docs and editor config -----------------------------------------
# Not referenced by the build. Kept out to reduce context size.
.vscode/
.vscode-test/
jest.config.ts
.oxlintrc.json
.prettierrc
README.md

# --- logs and editor temp files ---------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vs/
*.pid
